de_DE-thorsten-medium: a German voice for the Piper text to speech system,
copied unchanged from https://huggingface.co/rhasspy/piper-voices
(de/de_DE/thorsten/medium/). Its model card (MODEL_CARD in this folder)
names the dataset, the licence and the model it started from.

Recordings: Thorsten-Voice by Thorsten Müller,
https://github.com/thorstenMueller/Thorsten-Voice, released under
CC0 1.0 Universal (public domain dedication),
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode

Lineage, as far as the model cards say: the voice was fine-tuned from the
rdh base model (medium quality; nl_BE, one Flemish speaker, CC0); its card
is copied here too (nl/nl_BE/rdh/medium/MODEL_CARD). The voices repository
rhasspy/piper-voices is published under the MIT licence.

No non-commercial condition applies as far as these cards say: the voice
and what it speaks may be used for any purpose. Credit is not required
by CC0, but orOS names Thorsten Müller and the Piper voices project where
the voice is downloaded.

orOS downloads this folder on the person's device only when they ask for
the natural German voice. Nothing in it was changed.
